    "title": "Final Injury Report for Timberwolves-Celtics: Will Jaylen Brown, Anthony Edwards Play?",
    "text": "The Boston Celtics are at home on Sunday night as they host the Minnesota Timberwolves in an interconference showdown.Boston enters Sunday’s game with a 47-23 record after defeating the Memphis Grizzlies on the road on Friday night.AdvertisementBoston Celtics guard/forward Jaylen Brown (7)© Brian Fluharty-Imagn Images (© Brian Fluharty-Imagn Images)In Friday’s victory over the Grizzlies, Jaylen Brown led the way for the Celtics as he recorded 30 points, six rebounds and six assists while Luka Garza added 22 points and seven rebounds of his own off the bench.Now Boston will try to grab another victory on Sunday as they face off against the Timberwolves in a tough home matchup.On the other side, Minnesota enters Sunday’s contest with a 43-28 record after losing at home to the Portland Trail Blazers on Friday night.AdvertisementMinnesota Timberwolves center Rudy Gobert (27)Matt Blewett-Imagn Images (Matt Blewett-Imagn Images)Rudy Gobert led the way for the Timberwolves in Friday’s loss as he ended the game with 18 points and 15 rebounds while Ayo Dosunmu recorded 17 points, 10 rebounds and eight assists.While both teams are looking to pick up a victory in Sunday night’s matchup, both squads may be without multiple key players due to injuries.For the Timberwolves, they have two players listed on their injury report for Sunday’s game in Boston.AdvertisementMinnesota Timberwolves guard Anthony Edwards (5) © Jesse Johnson-Imagn Images (© Jesse Johnson-Imagn Images)Minnesota has ruled out Anthony Edwards due to right knee patellofemoral pain syndrome as he will miss his fourth consecutive contest and he is expected to miss at least one week due to the injury.Minnesota @Timberwolves Status Report in advance of tomorrow night’s game at Boston Celtics:QUESTIONABLE Reid- Right Ankle SprainOUTEdwards- Right Knee Patellofemoral Pain SyndromeFreeman- Two-WayZikarsky- Two-Way— Timberwolves PR (@Twolves_PR) March 21, 2026With Edwards still sidelined, Dosunmu, Donte DiVincenzo and Bones Hyland could all continue to have larger roles.The Timberwolves have listed Naz Reid as questionable due to a right ankle sprain and he is in danger of missing his third consecutive contest.AdvertisementCredit: Matt Blewett-Imagn Images (Credit&colon; Matt Blewett-Imagn Images)If Reid remains sidelined, Kyle Anderson, Terrence Shannon Jr. and Joan Beringer could all be in line for increased roles.Celtics Injury Report: Will Jaylen Brown Play?On the other side, the Celtics have two players listed on their injury report for Sunday, including Brown.Boston Celtics guard Jaylen BrownKevin Jairaj-Imagn Images (Kevin Jairaj-Imagn Images)Boston has listed Brown as probable due to a left quad contusion and he is expected to play against the Timberwolves.Injury Report for tomorrow vs. MIN:Jaylen Brown - Left Quad Contusion - PROBABLENikola Vucevic - Right Ring Finger Fracture - OUT— Boston Celtics (@celtics) March 21, 2026The Celtics have ruled out Nikola Vucevic as he remains sidelined while recovering from surgery to repair a fracture in his right ring finger.AdvertisementBoston Celtics center Nikola Vucevic (4)Mark J. Rebilas-Imagn Images (Mark J&period; Rebilas-Imagn Images)Fans can catch Sunday night’s matchup between the Timberwolves and Celtics from Boston at 8:00 p.m. ET on NBC and Peacock.This story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Mar 22, 2026, where it first appeared in the NBA section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
